Identify stakeholders – Determine who will use, manage, or be affected by the system.

Gather requirements – Collect information through interviews, surveys, observations, questionnaires, or discussions.

Analyze requirements – Understand and clarify what the users actually need.

Define functional requirements – Specify what the system should do.

Define non-functional requirements – Specify qualities such as performance, security, reliability, usability, and scalability.

Identify constraints – Consider limitations involving budget, technology, time, resources, and regulations.

Prioritize requirements – Separate essential requirements from optional or future features.

Document requirements – Prepare a clear requirements document, often called a Software Requirements Specification (SRS).
